<title>LATVIA: SWAP AUCTION RATE DOWN THIRD CONSECUTIVE WEEK.</title>
<headline>SWAP AUCTION RATE DOWN THIRD CONSECUTIVE WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central bank said on Tuesday that the lat/dollar swap auction rate fell for the third consecutive week to 4.51 percent against 4.61 percent on August 12.</p>
<p>One commercial bank participated in the auction, with three million lats offered and sold, the central bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
